# Frontend — Angular Standards

## Baseline
- Angular v17+ with standalone components. TypeScript `strict: true` in `tsconfig.json`.
- No `any`. Every API response has an interface in `shared/models/`
  (`profile.model.ts`, `query.model.ts`, `recommendation.model.ts`). Field names match the
  backend JSON exactly (snake_case as defined in the spec).

## Services (no HttpClient in components)
- All HTTP calls live in `core/services/` (`ProfileService`, `QueryService`,
  `PipelineService`). Components inject services; they never inject `HttpClient`.
- Base URL comes from `environment.apiUrl`; never hardcode `http://localhost:5000`.
- Service methods return typed Observables: `Observable<Profile>`, never Promises,
  never `toPromise()` / `firstValueFrom()` for API data.

```ts
// ✅ GOOD
getProfile(uuid: string): Observable<Profile> {
  return this.http.get<Profile>(`${environment.apiUrl}/api/v1/profiles/${uuid}`);
}
// ❌ BAD — component calling HttpClient, untyped, Promise-based
await this.http.get(url).toPromise();
```

## Errors
- Handle HTTP errors with `catchError` in RxJS pipelines. Convert to a user-friendly
  message shown in the UI and via MatSnackBar. `console.error` alone is not acceptable.

## Data fetching and state
- Fetch data in an Angular Resolver or in component `ngOnInit` (spec allows either).
- Shared state across components uses Angular Signals or `BehaviorSubject`.
- Unsubscribe correctly (async pipe, `takeUntilDestroyed`, or `takeUntil`).

## Routing
- Routes in `app.routes.ts`. Dashboard, Profiles, and Queries are lazy-loaded
  (`loadComponent` / `loadChildren`).

## Forms
- Reactive Forms only (`FormGroup` / `FormControl` / `FormBuilder`). No `ngModel`
  template-driven forms anywhere.
- Validators live with the form definition; custom validators (e.g. domain format) are
  reusable functions, not inline logic in templates.

## No mock data
- No hardcoded arrays, fake stats, or placeholder records. Empty data shows an empty state.
